---
description: Use TestCommon files for shared module-specific test fixture builders.
globs: '**/*.test.ts,**/*.test.tsx'
alwaysApply: true
---

When multiple test files (even across directories) need the same fixture builder
for a specific module's types, extract it to a `XXXTestCommon.ts` file adjacent
to the primary module rather than duplicating the helper.

This is distinct from `FakeData`/`ClientFakeData` in `lib/testUtilities/` —
those provide general-purpose model builders. TestCommon files provide
module-specific test fixtures whose shape is tightly coupled to the module's
types and test data files.

## Example

```typescript
// lib/pdf/combineFilesIntoPDFTestCommon.ts

import type { EvidenceSection } from './evidence/evidenceTransform';

export function _makeTestEvidenceSections<DataT>(files: {
  passport: DataT;
  birthCertificate: DataT;
  travelHistory: DataT;
  passportStamps: DataT;
}): EvidenceSection<DataT>[] {
  return [
    { title: 'Photo identification (passport)', /* ... */ },
    { title: 'Birth certificate', /* ... */ },
    // ...
  ];
}
```

```typescript
// lib/pdf/combineFilesIntoPDF.test.ts — imports from common
import { _makeTestEvidenceSections } from './combineFilesIntoPDFTestCommon';

// lib/pdf/evidence/generateEvidencePDFs.test.ts — imports from common
import { _makeTestEvidenceSections } from '../combineFilesIntoPDFTestCommon';
```

## Naming

- File: `XXXTestCommon.ts` adjacent to the primary non-test module
- Exports: underscore-prefixed (`_make*`) to signal testing-only use, consistent
  with the codebase convention